WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.583
MARK MIRCHANDANI:
Today, we're talking

00:00:01.583 --> 00:00:04.480
about Anthos and AWS, supporting
health care providers,

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:06.097
and Google Cloud training.

00:00:06.097 --> 00:00:07.930
I'm Mark, and welcome
to this week in Cloud,

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:09.880
where we serve you
the lowest latency

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.250
news from the safety of home.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:14.530
Anthos was announced
with an ambitious goal

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:16.329
to enable portability
for applications

00:00:16.329 --> 00:00:19.115
across your multi-cloud
or hybrid infrastructure.

00:00:19.115 --> 00:00:21.490
Over the past year, we've been
working hard and expanding

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:23.380
support for multi-cloud,
and we've just

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:26.427
graduated AWS support
to generally available.

00:00:26.427 --> 00:00:28.510
We'll continue to provide
flexible Cloud computing

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:31.090
solutions so that your
business can grow and adapt

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:33.310
to whatever comes its way.

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:35.600
As the health care industry
is pushed to its limits,

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.600
we're focusing on offering
support and solutions

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.160
wherever we can.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:41.740
From offering HIPAA compliant
telehealth services with Google

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:44.140
Meet, to providing Google
Cloud research credits,

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:47.930
and hosting a free repository
of public health care data sets.

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:50.050
And finally, we've released
our Cloud health care

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:52.690
API as generally available
to help organizations

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:56.830
ingest and manage key data
from a variety of systems.

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:59.410
Cloud Spanner provides a
scalable, multi-version

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:01.900
database with
relational semantics.

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:04.390
We've just introduced
managed backup-restore

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:07.540
to provide data protection with
minimal management overhead.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:10.210
These restores are
optimized for data access,

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:12.790
meaning that you can access
terabytes of restore data

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:14.620
within minutes of a failure.

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:17.650
Check out the post to learn more
and to see other new features

00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:19.355
in Spanner.

00:01:19.355 --> 00:01:20.980
When it comes to
Google Cloud training,

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:24.010
we focused on creating content
for all learning styles,

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:27.130
from self-paced courses to
instructor-led workshops.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:29.530
While in-person learning
isn't possible right now,

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:32.297
we're focusing on creating
virtual classrooms.

00:01:32.297 --> 00:01:33.880
Check out Cloud
training to learn more

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:35.680
about enrolling
in a virtual class

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:38.007
and to see all of
the courses we offer.

00:01:38.007 --> 00:01:40.090
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:42.410
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:43.610
Have any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:45.530
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:48.090
We'll see you in the Cloud.

